# meshtk is a VANILLA upstream checkout. This repo tracks con-specific CONFIG
# ONLY — never Go source.
#
# How the image gets built (apps/build.sh:148-169, resolve_meshtk):
#   CI    clone github.com/whereiskurt/meshtk, then overlay every file
#         `git ls-files` reports under this directory on top of it.
#   local use apps/run.mqtt/meshtk/ directly as the Docker context.
#
# Tracked-ness is therefore LOAD-BEARING in CI: a file present on disk but
# untracked is silently discarded by the fresh-clone step and never ships.
# Adding a con-specific file means allowlisting it here, not just creating it.
#
# The inverse is equally true and is why this list is short: anything tracked
# here SHADOWS upstream forever. It must be hand-mirrored on every change and
# can silently drift. Go source was tracked here until 2026-08-01 — 105 files,
# every one byte-identical to upstream, i.e. pure redundancy carrying pure
# drift risk. Do not put Go source back.
#
# Gitignore mechanics: un-ignoring a directory does NOT un-ignore its contents,
# so each level below is re-ignored with `dir/*` before the next `!` allows a
# specific child through. Skipping a re-ignore line silently exposes an entire
# subtree as untracked-but-present, which reads as clean locally and then
# vanishes in CI.
meshtk/*

# --- Con config: images, versions, fleet definition -------------------------
!meshtk/Dockerfile.meshtk
!meshtk/VERSION
!meshtk/meshtk.dc34.yaml
!meshtk/meshtk.localdev.yaml

# --- Fleet node seeds (pinned ghost/rabbit identities, PKI, positions) ------
!meshtk/nodes.ghost.*.json
!meshtk/nodes.rabbit.*.json

# --- Descend toward the two things below that are genuinely ours ------------
!meshtk/internal/
meshtk/internal/*

# --- Con GPX routes ---------------------------------------------------------
# NOTE: embedded.go is deliberately NOT tracked. It used to be, carrying a
# local //go:embed patch that vendor-sync clobbered twice and silently stranded
# all 24 GPX sim nodes at 0,0 (#1009, fixed by #1028/#1029). Upstream now uses
# `//go:embed */*.gpx`, correct in both trees because go:embed only errors on a
# pattern matching NOTHING — so these routes are picked up with no patched Go
# file to maintain. See whereiskurt/meshtk#35.
!meshtk/internal/embedded/
meshtk/internal/embedded/*
!meshtk/internal/embedded/gpx/
meshtk/internal/embedded/gpx/*
!meshtk/internal/embedded/gpx/*/
meshtk/internal/embedded/gpx/*/*
!meshtk/internal/embedded/gpx/*/*.gpx

# --- Con-specific test, the one deliberate exception to "no Go source" ------
# Guards the embed above: it asserts every GPXFile: in meshtk.dc34.yaml
# resolves, and runs with cwd set to its package dir so the .gpx files are NOT
# on the filesystem — exercising the go:embed fallback specifically. It has no
# upstream counterpart, so it MUST stay tracked or the CI overlay drops it and
# the regression it guards ships green.
!meshtk/internal/app/
meshtk/internal/app/*
!meshtk/internal/app/fleet/
meshtk/internal/app/fleet/*
!meshtk/internal/app/fleet/gpx_routes_test.go
